          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 555574210,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "L/R desync is strange as there is no difference between Play/Pause code except Pause calls Pause on Qt media library. L/R channel is created by OS/soundcard, not by Wireshark so I'm afraid it is somewhere else than in Wireshark.\nFor curiosity, are you playing just two channels therefore L/R difference is audible or did you tried e.g. 10 channels and all L are shifted to all R channels? The point is that player runs every RTP stream on its own therefore I expect that for 10 channels you will hear 10 slightly shifted replays. In this case I'm quite confident it is not in Wireshark.\nYou can verify it if you save it as .au/.wav in RTP Player - it saves what is replayed. I expect that channels there will be aligned correctly and issue is observed just during reply...",
          "author": {
            "id": 7791033,
            "username": "j.novak",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "j.novak@netsystem.cz",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b98b9c10d87ea9f383019b704e727c94ba6895dd3c46291d23e400738e1c6f1d?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/j.novak"
          },
